Prior to the global financial crisis there was no clear requirement for central clearing of OTC derivatives. Calls for central clearing emerged globally after Bear Stearns. G20 leaders agreed in Pittsburgh in 2009 on requirements including:
• all standardised OTC derivatives to be traded on exchanges or electronic platforms;
• mandatory central clearing of standardised OTC derivatives;
• reporting of OTC derivatives to trade repositories; and
• higher capital requirements for non-centrally cleared OTC derivatives.

