Risk budgeting is the process of allocating and managing risks to different
aspects of the investment process using a \term{top-down} approach. The budget
helps the organization stay on course with respect to its risk plan. There are
two types:

\begin{itemize}
\item Budgeting \term{across asset classes};
\item Budgeting \term{across asset managers}.
\end{itemize}

blocks.plain_text:
Risk budgeting is the process of allocating and managing risks to different aspects of the investment process using a top-down approach. The budget helps the organization stay on course with respect to its risk plan. There are two types:
• Budgeting across asset classes;
• Budgeting across asset managers.

